Fate, it seems, favors those with stupid names.

Moron Dragonfodder VIII, a neutral human Tourist, entered the Dungeon
of Doom soft and weak, ignorant of the greatness he would achieve
before it was all over.  On dungeon level 2, he found two crossaligned
altars and, converting both, established a stash there.  Also on level
2 was an armor store, from which he procured a pair of Gauntlets of
Power as well as some crappy armor.  Soon afterward, through piety and
mass bribes in the form of freshly slain corpses, Moron was rewarded
with the Magicbane.  Descending to the next level, he found and cleaned
out a delicatessen and discovered a Wand of Wishing.  (I don't remember
what exactly he wished for, because I forgot to write it down, and I
took a long break in the middle of this game.)
Taking a detour to Minetown, Moron was pleased to find a co-aligned
altar.  After his foray into the Gnomish Mines, Moron found another
altar on level 6, which he quickly converted to Neutrality, and moved
his stash to a closet adjoining the altar, where it would remain for
the rest of the game.
Moron's shopping tour continued as he found an armor store on Level 10,
which yielded the Mjollnir and a blessed +1 Helm of Brilliance.
Deciding that some holy water was in order, Moron performed a water
prayer and was crowned the Envoy of Balance.  Of course, having a
better weapon already, he put the Vorpal Blade away in his stash.
Moron ran into problems on level 12, where he cleared out a leprechaun
hall and snacked on the corpses--forgetting that leprechauns don't give
the teleport control intrinsic.  Dealing for the moment with his
teleportitis, Moron discovered a co-aligned church on level 14.  Soon
after, he tamed a troll and a rock troll and, with their help,
extracted enough funds from the establishments he had visited to get
his protection maxed out.  On a side note, the troll was later lost and
the rock troll whistled into a polymorph trap, becoming a vampire lord.
Moron soon reached the point where he could no longer tolerate
teleporting around at random, and hunted for tengus to obtain teleport
control.  During his quest for tengu flesh, he found a few wraith
corpses, and his vampire lord died in a valiant attempt on a fire
elemental's life.  Eventually, he was forced to resort to writing two
cursed scrolls of genocide.
With controlled teleports on his side, Moron proceeded to thoroughly
thrash the Master of Thieves and progress down into Gehennom.  Progress
in Gehennom went smoothly, especially after Moron decided to put his
magic marker collection to use and get his AC up (down) to -33.  He
came to find the sealife lurking in moats an eyesore, so he blessed
genocided ;.  R followed after a disenchanter reduced his silver saber
from +7 to +6.
Now, Moron had fallen down lots of holes and trapdoors on his way
through Gehennom.  As a consequence, going back up to collect candles,
he had to do battle with all the demon lords he bypassed.  They were
quickly vanquished.  On the way, he tamed a warhorse using a carrot and
whistled it onto a trap until it came out a yellow dragon.
Finding a vibrating square at the bottom of Gehennom, Moron lit up the
Candelabrum before realizing that he lacked the Book of the Dead.  This
situation was quickly rectified, and Moron, in possession of the Amulet
of Yendor, fought his way up.  Sadly, the yellow dragon perished.
Taking a break from his frantic rush to the surface at his stash, Moron
picked up some diamonds, blessed and drank his collection of potions of
gain level, and made some additional potions of full healing.
Bashing his way through the Planes, Moron arrived on the Astral Plane
and was joined in his final battle by a guardian Angel of The Lady.  He
tried the rightmost room first--nope--but found sanctuary, and his
coaligned altar, in the central room.  Success!

